Z||000000||FieroJoe||12-25-2000||12:01 PM||||To anybody who has refinished 14" Hi Tech rims, is the gray area that is "in" the spokes painted?  I know that I must remove all the clear coat of the machined surfaces of the rim, for that is what is going to be polished, but will I have to worry about the other parts, as in will the stripper harm them?<P><P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||JohnnyK||12-25-2000||12:24 PM||||Yup.. I decided to take off the grey paint, however, it is a pain to get, so there is still lots in there on mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||12-25-2000||07:48 PM||||Do they still look pretty good with that paint mostly gone?  I was wondering if the contrast would make the polished part stand out more.<P>Post a pic if you can!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-26-2000||09:41 PM||||There was a picture here someplace of those wheels sans paint. They look pretty bad.<P>If you use one of the thick paste like strippers then you can control where it goes better. This would let you get the clear coat off the AL with minimal damage to the painted inner area.<P>Last set I did I stripped like above and then polished them up with Mothers. Looked a hell of alot better than crappy clear coat.<P>Even if you do the whole wheel the pastes are better. Also stick the wheel in a plastic bag so it doesn't dry out so fast.||||reg||1
